    <h1 class="article-title" style="margin-bottom:1.75rem;">About Me</h1>

    <p>
      QA Coach with <strong>10+ years of experience</strong> in outsourcing and product companies,
      including projects in corporate security, fintech, and blockchain.
    </p>

    <p>
      Trained <strong>40+ QA Leads</strong> both individually and in groups, and over
      <strong>100 QA specialists</strong> at various levels. Have been mentoring and consulting
      for 8 years, with 4+ years at the team lead and director level.
      I use coaching to help people unlock their inner potential.
    </p>

    <p>Speaker and moderator at QA events — online and offline.</p>

    <h2>Projects</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>
        Co-author of the <a href="https://spoti.fi/3LAku0Q" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Testing Minutes</strong></a> podcast
      </li>
      <li>
        Author of <a href="https://t.me/a_grygorenko" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Нотатки суворого QA</strong></a> —
        one of the largest Ukrainian Telegram channels about QA
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong><a href="/talks">Speaker</a></strong> at Ministry of Testing and other QA conferences
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Mentoring & Consulting</h2>

    <p>
      Achieving professional and personal goals can be challenging — regardless of your experience or position.
      As a coach and mentor, I help testers, managers, and developers who want to grow
      and reach new heights in their career.
    </p>

    <p><strong>My goal:</strong></p>
    <ol>
      <li>Help you reconnect with the skills and knowledge you already have.</li>
      <li>Give you the confidence to apply that knowledge in real situations and take the right next steps in your career.</li>
    </ol>

    <p><strong>Who I work with:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>QA Leads, QA Managers, Test Managers</strong> — building or fixing testing processes,
        optimizing quality assurance, avoiding the mistakes that slow down your team's growth.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Testers</strong> — resume review, interview prep, creating a personal development plan,
        or figuring out where to go next in your career.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Project Managers & Developers</strong> — structuring quality processes without a dedicated
        QA team, integrating quality thinking at every stage of the project.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>How it works:</strong></p>
    <p>
      The first meeting is <strong>free</strong>. We get to know each other, discuss your challenges,
      and I'll already help you tackle some of them on the spot.
      If we see a path forward together — we continue.
    </p>

